user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 5,
    "feature": {
      "name": "distinct_factual_premises_challenged_count",
      "dtype": "numeric",
      "source_columns": [
        "title",
        "argument",
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Counter-argument comments (OC_comments, not OP) read against the OP title/argument: number of distinct factual premises of the OP's argument that are challenged by at least one comment",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title, argument and OC_comments jointly. Identify the distinct factual (empirical/descriptive, not value, logical-structure or definitional) premises stated in the OP's title/argument. Count how many distinct such premises are explicitly challenged (disputed as false, unsupported, or inaccurate with factual argument) by at least one comment in OC_comments. Count each premise once even if several comments challenge it; do not count the same premise twice for rewordings. Do not count challenges to values, reasoning, or conclusions only, nor agreement, concessions, or comments challenging things the OP did not claim. Ignore the OP's later edits only if clearly marked as edits; do not use conversation. Output a non-negative integer (0 = comments assessable and none challenge a factual premise). Null if OC_comments is empty/unparseable or argument is missing."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 7,
    "feature": {
      "name": "distinct_counterargument_count",
      "dtype": "numeric",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments",
        "title",
        "argument"
      ],
      "definition": "Other users' comments in OC_comments: number of distinct counter-arguments (semantically distinct challenges to the OP's view) posted across the comments",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read title and argument (for the OP's claim) and OC_comments (JSON list of comments by users other than OP; order carries no meaning). Count the distinct counter-arguments against the OP's view across all comments: each separate line of reasoning/challenge counts once; the same argument repeated in several comments or restated within a comment counts once; comments that are not counter-arguments (agreement, jokes, questions only, moderator/bot notices, pure clarification) count zero. Do not use the conversation column or later replies. Output a non-negative integer. 0 if the list is valid but empty or has no counter-arguments. Null if OC_comments is missing or unparseable."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
